# Code owners — review routing.
#
# PLACEHOLDER. @CasualOffice/maintainers does not exist yet. GitHub silently
# ignores an owner entry that names a non-existent team or a user without write
# access: the file parses, the rules simply never match, and nothing is ever
# requested for review. Until the team is created in the CasualOffice
# organisation and given write access to this repository, this file assigns
# nobody. Treat it as inert, not as coverage.
#
# Two things must happen for it to take effect:
#   1. create the @CasualOffice/maintainers team and grant it write access;
#   2. enable "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch protection rule
#      for `main`.
# Until (2), an owner review is advisory even once (1) is done.
#
# Later, split this file by area — auth, policy, data model and search each want
# different reviewers. One blanket team is the right starting point precisely
# because it is honest about the current size of the team; a fake split creates
# the appearance of specialist review that is not happening.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                       @CasualOffice/maintainers

# The specification. Each document is authoritative for exactly one concern
# (docs/README.md §1), so a docs change is a contract change and gets the same
# scrutiny as code.
/docs/                  @CasualOffice/maintainers

# All Rust crates.
/crates/                @CasualOffice/maintainers

# Schema. Forward-only, and every tenant-scoped table needs RLS in the same
# migration — the two mistakes that are expensive after they ship.
/migrations/            @CasualOffice/maintainers

# The gates themselves. A change here can disable enforcement everywhere else,
# which is the one category of change that must never be self-merged.
/.github/               @CasualOffice/maintainers
/deny.toml              @CasualOffice/maintainers
/clippy.toml            @CasualOffice/maintainers
/rust-toolchain.toml    @CasualOffice/maintainers

# The rules of engagement.
/CLAUDE.md              @CasualOffice/maintainers
/CONTRIBUTING.md        @CasualOffice/maintainers
/SECURITY.md            @CasualOffice/maintainers
